&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Location: Taipei, Taiwan&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fast-Frogward Your Career to Years From Now&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Be part of a team where your work directly shapes the way the world’s top companies build and secure their software. At JFrog, as an Account Executive, Enterprise (Taiwan) you’ll play a key role in bringing our industry-leading solutions to market, helping customers like Amazon, Google, and Netflix solve their most pressing DevSecOps and AI/ML challenges. Every day offers new opportunities to collaborate, strategize, and innovate in a fast-paced, growth-driven culture. If you thrive in a dynamic environment and want to make an impact in the world of software, JFrog is the place for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be doing as an Account Executive, Enterprise:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you’ll be a key player in our fast-paced and highly innovative Sales team. You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sell JFrog’s platform to leading Taiwan and China to Global (C2G) enterprises&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop new business, bring in new logos by hunting across verticals directly and Via partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong relationships with key stakeholders in enterprises&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop DevOps strategies with C-level executives, work with CISOs on their security priorities and goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceed monthly, quarterly, and annual sales targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel to customer locations to support sales efforts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with the SE, CS and consulting teams to achieve product adoption&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;If you don’t meet 100% of the requirements below – that’s okay, nobody’s perfect! We believe in hiring people, not just a list of skills. We encourage you to apply if you think this is a role that would make you excited about coming to work every day.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring to the table:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Taiwan large enterprise customers and reseller/ecosystem of software business, especially in FSI, High-tech manufacturing, gaming industries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with C2G enterprise customers and reseller/ecosystem of software business, especially in Web3, manufacturing, e-commerce industries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of proven experience in field of enterprise software and solutions sales, selling to end-users as well as VPs and C-level executives across multiple departments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding and experience in managing the complete sales cycle from prospecting to closure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A good understanding of SaaS sales processes and management of key KPIs is desirable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Goal-oriented with a proven track record of consistently exceeding the sales quota in previous positions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work as part of a fast-paced team while demonstrating flexibility, reliability, and taking initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills in English; ability to explain technological strategies to both end-users and decision-makers throughout organizations, including technical, business, and C-level audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer-success mentality, with a winning attitude&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An energized and enthusiastic, self-motivated, competitive, creative problem-solving, relationship builder, customer-focused and highly responsive leader&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in business administration, marketing, or technical discipline; MBA is an advantage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must have a good understanding of technology in general, understanding how to sell to technical stakeholders, especially around DevOps, security, and SaaS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position is based in Taipei, and candidate is willing to travel to meet with customers/resellers in the region each quarter.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About JFrog:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;JFrog is the only end-to-end software supply chain platform that provides complete visibility, security, and control for automating the delivery of trusted releases from code to production. Our platform enables organizations to manage, secure, and automate their software delivery process, fueling innovation without worry. We empower companies to build and release software faster and more securely than ever before.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With over 7,500 customers worldwide, including many Fortune 100 companies, JFrog is at the forefront of global innovation. Join us in shaping the future of software delivery and contributing to solutions that empower some of the world&#39;s most influential industries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Here’s what our employees have to say about working at JFrog:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;&quot;I wanted to work in a company that takes technology forward.&quot;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;&quot;Our business is so interesting because it is constantly moving, and we have to adapt new solutions to the challenges that arise from the customers.&quot;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;&quot;It’s nice to work for a company with a must-have product, not a nice-to-have.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;#LI-REMOTE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At JFrog, we’re reinventing DevSecOps to help the world’s greatest companies innovate.&amp;nbsp;Our team of industry-leading software security experts is a true pioneer, constantly pushing the boundaries with original research and technological innovation.&amp;nbsp;JFrog is a special place with a unique combination of brilliance, spirit, and just all-around great people.&amp;nbsp;Thousands of customers, including the majority of the Fortune 100, trust JFrog to manage, accelerate, and secure their software delivery from code to production – a concept we call “liquid software”. Wouldn&#39;t it be amazing if you could join us on our journey?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our business is growing fast, and we’re looking for a sharp Revenue Assistant Controller to grow with it. You’ll work with people across the organization, help shape our revenue accounting, revenue policy and compliance, lead projects in accounting, business and process automation – including using AI tools to make the way we work smarter, faster and leaner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a Revenue Assistant Controller at JFrog you will…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Support the month-end close: monthly revenue recognition and commission capitalization under ASC 606, revenue analytics and deferred revenue reconciliations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Become one of the finance team’s go-to revenue accounting experts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Team up with Sales, Sales Operations, AR, IS and Legal to support the business’s ongoing revenue recognition and ARR needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Spot opportunities to improve, and partner with other teams to simplify revenue processes and build best practices and controls across the company – including using AI tools to automate and speed up day-to-day work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Review contracts and apply the right revenue recognition method and ARR treatment, in line with accounting standards and our revenue recognition policy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Help keep our revenue recognition policy up to date – every year, and whenever the business needs it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Work hand in hand with our SOX team and external auditors to make sure approved revenue policies are followed and monitored, and prepare the schedules and reports for the annual audit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Jump in on ad hoc projects, both revenue- and business-related&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To be a Revenue Assistant Controller at JFrog you need...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; CPA with Big 4 experience, ideally in SaaS audit or professional practice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Solid knowledge of ASC 606 revenue recognition&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Tech industry experience, especially in a revenue team, is an advantage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Detail-oriented, with strong analytical and problem-solving skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; A great communicator and business partner who works easily across teams and at every level of the company&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Highly proficient in Excel, with hands-on experience using AI tools to analyze data, automate tasks and work smarter&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp; &amp;nbsp; Experience with systems like NetSuite, Salesforce, Zuora, and BI dashboards (Tableau), is an advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At JFrog, we’re reinventing DevOps to help the world’s greatest companies innovate -- and we want you along for the ride. This is a special place with a unique combination of brilliance, spirit and just all-around great people. Here, if you’re willing to do more, your career can take off. And since software plays a central role in everyone’s lives, you’ll be part of an important mission. Thousands of customers, including the majority of the Fortune 100, trust JFrog to manage, accelerate, and secure their software delivery from code to production -- a concept we call “liquid software.” Wouldn&#39;t it be amazing if you could join us in our journey?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a meticulous, proactive, and collaborative teammate to join our Renewals team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an &lt;strong&gt;Associate Account Manager, Revenue Retention&lt;/strong&gt; in JFrog you will be a key driver of the “Liquid Software” vision by ensuring our customers&#39; journey with JFrog remains seamless and uninterrupted. By mastering the renewals lifecycle, you enable the world&#39;s leading organizations to maintain their continuous delivery pipelines with confidence and speed. Your technical precision in account management ensures that the flow of innovation never stops, making you a vital architect of our customer retention and long-term success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As an Associate Account Manager, Revenue Retention, in JFrog you will...&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scale the renewals process by architecting accurate quotes and opportunities across a targeted global portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive operational excellence by collaborating with Finance, Legal, and Deal Desk to ensure 100% contract accuracy and compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maximize customer retention by proactively managing the end-to-end renewal lifecycle within your assigned territory, including tracking pending signatures through to close and understanding the downstream consequences of a lapsed renewal (especially on usage-based and cloud products) well enough to create urgency with the customer without being prompted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize Salesforce data integrity to provide real-time visibility into renewal health and territory performance, recognizing that clean, current data is the direct input to the AI-driven renewal risk scoring this team runs on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accelerate business growth by identifying expansion opportunities and providing actionable insights during the renewal cycle using AI-assisted signal review (Gong call analysis, renewal risk scoring) to surface expansion opportunities before they show up in a standard pipeline review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recognize strategic deal signals and streamline the customer experience by orchestrating high-touch communications and owning contract and legal-adjacent processes end-to-end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Approach the renewal motion as something actively evolving with AI-assisted tooling, ready to take on higher-complexity, higher-touch accounts as routine tiers become more automated.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To be an Associate Account Manager, Revenue Retention&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;in JFrog you need...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A minimum of 4 years of relevant experience in account management, renewals, or sales operations within a SaaS environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of managing high-volume portfolios and meeting tight deadlines with exceptional attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency in Salesforce (SFDC) and the MS Office Suite, particularly Excel, including working deal math independently: discount deltas, co-term pricing across tiers, and monthly-vs-annual savings comparisons.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated problem-solving skills with the ability to navigate complex internal processes and cross-functional dependencies, including contract and legal workflow literacy (JSA, DPA, NDA, compliance routing).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication skills to effectively engage with both internal stakeholders and external customer liaisons.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a fast-paced, high-growth technical environment where adaptability and a “Froggy” spirit are essential, with working depth on the JFrog platform itself (Xray, edge nodes, tiering) enough to handle a technical objection without a one-line script.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI fluency for non-technical, customer-facing work: using AI to accelerate research and drafting, then verifying the output before treating it as finished.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT JFROG CAN OFFER…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At JFrog, base salary is only one component of our compensation package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position has a base salary range between $90,000 to $115,000. &amp;nbsp;Base salary will be based on your skills, qualifications, experience and location.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additionally, this role may be eligible for discretionary bonuses or commission payments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position also includes an equity package of restricted stock units (RSU). &amp;nbsp;In addition, JFrog employees are eligible to participate in our Employee Stock Purchase Plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JFrog provides employees comprehensive benefits including medical, dental, vision, retirement, wellness and much more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JFrog embraces hybrid work: 3 days in office / 2 days remote.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;JFrog is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation, national origin or nationality, ancestry, age, disability, gender identity or expression, marital status or any other category protected by law.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At JFrog, we’re reinventing DevOps to help the world’s greatest companies innovate -- and we want you along for the ride. This is a special place with a unique combination of brilliance, spirit and just all-around great people. Here, if you’re willing to do more, your career can take off. And since software plays a central role in everyone’s lives, you’ll be part of an important mission. Thousands of customers, including the majority of the Fortune 100, trust JFrog to manage, accelerate, and secure their software delivery from code to production -- a concept we call “liquid software.” Wouldn&#39;t it be amazing if you could join us in our journey?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a meticulous, proactive, and collaborative to join our Renewals team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will be a key driver of the &quot;Liquid Software&quot; vision by ensuring our customers&#39; journey with JFrog remains seamless and uninterrupted. By mastering the renewals lifecycle, you enable the world&#39;s leading organizations to maintain their continuous delivery pipelines with confidence and speed. Your technical precision in account management ensures that the flow of innovation never stops, making you a vital architect of our customer retention and long-term success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a Customer Retention Associate Account Manager in JFrog you will...&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scale the renewals process by architecting accurate quotes and opportunities across a targeted global portfolio.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive operational excellence by collaborating with Finance, Legal, and Deal Desk to ensure 100% contract accuracy and compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maximize customer retention by proactively managing the end-to-end renewal lifecycle within your assigned territory.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize Salesforce data integrity to provide real-time visibility into renewal health and territory performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accelerate business growth by identifying expansion opportunities and providing actionable insights during the renewal cycle leading with AI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Streamline the customer experience by orchestrating high-touch communications and resolving complex back-office administrative tasks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To be a &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Customer Retention Associate Account Manager &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;in JFrog you need...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A minimum of 4 years of relevant experience in account management, renewals, or sales operations within a SaaS environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of managing high-volume portfolios and meeting tight deadlines with exceptional attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency in Salesforce (SFDC) and the MS Office Suite, particularly Excel for data tracking and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated problem-solving skills with the ability to navigate complex internal processes and cross-functional dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication skills to effectively engage with both internal stakeholders and external customer liaisons.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a fast-paced, high-growth technical environment where adaptability and a &quot;Froggy&quot; spirit are essential.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT JFROG CAN OFFER…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At JFrog, base salary is only one component of our compensation package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position has a base salary range between $75,000 to $90,000. &amp;nbsp;Base salary will be based on your skills, qualifications, experience and location.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additionally, this role may be eligible for discretionary bonuses or commission payments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position also includes an equity package of restricted stock units (RSU). &amp;nbsp;In addition, JFrog employees are eligible to participate in our Employee Stock Purchase Plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JFrog provides employees comprehensive benefits including medical, dental, vision, retirement, wellness and much more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JFrog embraces hybrid work: 3 days in office / 2 days remote.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;JFrog is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation, national origin or nationality, ancestry, age, disability, gender identity or expression, marital status or any other category protected by law.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At JFrog, we’re reinventing DevOps to help the world’s greatest companies innovate -- and we want you along for the ride. This is a special place with a unique combination of brilliance, spirit and just all-around great people. Here, if you’re willing to do more, your career can take off. And since software plays a central role in everyone’s lives, you’ll be part of an important mission. Thousands of customers, including the majority of the Fortune 100, trust JFrog to manage, accelerate, and secure their software delivery from code to production -- a concept we call “liquid software.” Wouldn&#39;t it be amazing if you could join us in our journey?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a proactive, collaborative, and results-driven Associate HRBP to join our North America HR team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role you will act as a critical bridge for our individual contributors and managers across all US departments, ensuring our frogs are engaged, aligned, and empowered to deliver &quot;liquid software&quot; seamlessly. Partnering closely with two Senior HR Business Partners and the VP of HR North America, you will turn organizational goals into actionable initiatives that strengthen team resilience and culture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As an Associate HRBP at JFrog you will...&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with frogs and managers in helping them do their best work in alignment with our CODEX&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Focus on “sensing” to bring valuable insights to HR management and JFrog business units&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help our frogs throughout their journey at JFrog, collaborating with partners in other departments to ensure smooth transitions from onboarding to off boarding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Observe existing processes and data and suggest improvements that drive efficiency and value for the HR team and the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with the deployment of core HR initiatives throughout the year such as engagement, performance &amp;amp; talent management, change management, learning and development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the accuracy, timeliness and integrity of all HRIS updates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive special projects as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To be an Associate HRBP at JFrog you need...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Professional experience&lt;/strong&gt;: 4+ years of progressive HR experience, preferably within a fast-paced, high-tech software environment, showing a clear trajectory toward an HRBP path&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leveraging modern HR technologies and AI is highly valued&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relevant knowledge&lt;/strong&gt;: Familiarity with HR concepts, practices and programs, including relevant labor law.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelors/Masters degree in psychology or related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proactivity &amp;amp; curiosity&lt;/strong&gt;: Interest in deeply understanding our business and people, paired with a proactive mindset that anticipates talent risks, skills gaps and employee needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Relationship building &amp;amp; high EQ&lt;/strong&gt;: A proven track record of cultivating authentic relationships and influencing people. Possesses the emotional intelligence to serve as a grounded, human-centric anchor for teams navigating rapid change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Problem solving &amp;amp; adaptability&lt;/strong&gt;: The capacity to navigate a dynamic, fast-paced environment with decisive problem-solving. Ability to interpret people analytics and data-driven insights to make informed, evidence-backed recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration &amp;amp; communication&lt;/strong&gt;: Strong verbal and written communication skills with the ability to connect across diverse, cross-functional groups, translating organizational initiatives into clear, actionable guidance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT JFROG CAN OFFER…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At JFrog, base salary is only one component of our compensation package&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position has a base salary range between $120,000 to $135,000. &amp;nbsp;Base salary will be based on your skills, qualifications, experience and location&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position also includes an equity package of restricted stock units (RSU). &amp;nbsp;In addition, JFrog employees are eligible to participate in our Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JFrog provides employees comprehensive benefits including medical, dental, vision, retirement, wellness and much more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JFrog embraces hybrid work: 4 days in office / 1 days remote&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;JFrog is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation, national origin or nationality, ancestry, age, disability, gender identity or expression, marital status or any other category protected by law.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hybrid position, Monday–Friday&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At JFrog, we’re reinventing DevOps to help the world’s greatest companies innovate -- and we want you along for the ride. This is a special place with a unique combination of brilliance, spirit and just all-around great people. Here, if you’re willing to do more, your career can take off. And since software plays a central role in everyone’s lives, you’ll be part of an important mission. Join us on our journey!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a driven Business Development Representative to join our fast-growing Sales Development Unit. In this role, you will work closely with Marketing and Sales to help drive JFrog’s solutions. You will develop new business opportunities through outbound prospecting, cold calling, email campaigns, and inbound lead follow-up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a Business Development Representative at JFrog you will...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Internalize JFrog’s mission, vision, and values&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generate new business pipelines through outbound prospecting activities and inbound lead follow-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain sales data through Salesforce that will influence monthly/quarterly sales reports, pipelines, forecasts, etc&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research and evaluate prospects prior to engagement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish active communication and engagement with prospects to create new leads and sales opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with sales and marketing to build a sales strategy for generating new prospects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To be a Business Development Representative at JFrog you need...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;English native – Required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;German / Hebrew – advantage&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and interpersonal skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to multi-task and work in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Motivated by individual and team achievement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organized with the ability to multitask, prioritize, and manage time efficiently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Salesforce and use of sales acceleration tools like Outreach&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;234&quot; data-end=&quot;362&quot;&gt;Hybrid role (3 days in the office, 2 days remote), based in our London office at HYLO, 103–105 Bunhill Row, London EC1Y 8LZ.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At JFrog, we’re reinventing DevOps to help the world’s greatest companies innovate -- and we want you along for the ride. This is a special place with a unique combination of brilliance, spirit and just all-around great people. Here, if you’re willing to do more, your career can take off. And since software plays a central role in everyone’s lives, you’ll be part of an important mission. Join us on our journey!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a driven Business Development Representative to join our fast-growing Sales Development Unit. In this role, you will work closely with Marketing and Sales to help drive JFrog’s solutions. You will develop new business opportunities through outbound prospecting, cold calling, email campaigns, and inbound lead follow-up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a Business Development Representative at JFrog you will...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
