&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Deal Strategy Manager (APAC)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: Singapore&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fast-Frogward Your Career to Years From Now&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Be part of a team where your work directly shapes the way the world’s top companies build and secure their software. At JFrog, as a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Deal Strategy Manager, APAC&lt;/strong&gt; you’ll play a key role in bringing our industry-leading solutions to market, helping customers like Amazon, Google, and Netflix solve their most pressing DevSecOps and AI/ML challenges. Every day offers new opportunities to collaborate, strategize, and innovate in a fast-paced, growth-driven culture. If you thrive in a dynamic environment and want to make an impact in the world of software, JFrog is the place for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be doing as a Senior Deal Strategy Manager, APAC&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;JFrog is looking for a high-impact Senior Manager of Deal Strategy to serve as a strategic commercial architect and trusted advisor to our APAC Sales organization. In this critical role, you will partner with Sales Management to navigate large-scale, complex, and non-standard commercial structures, ensuring seamless execution while driving revenue growth. You will act as the central nexus between Sales, Finance, Legal, and Operations, building scalable frameworks that empower our leadership to make rapid, data-driven decisions in a fast-paced global environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In this role, you will...&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a strategic advisor to APAC Sales leadership, providing expert guidance on complex pricing, commercial terms, and deal architecture.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Account Executives to engineer commercial models and financial strategies for key strategic accounts.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the subject matter expert on revenue compliance and sales policies, advising teams on creative yet compliant contract solutions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner cross-functionally with Revenue, Finance, Legal, and Sales Operations to resolve complex billing, legal, or revenue recognition hurdles.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze deal trends and discounting patterns to optimize commercial performance across the APAC territory.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vet and refine escalation requests to ensure senior management focus remains on the most critical strategic priorities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;If you don’t meet 100% of the requirements below – that’s okay, nobody’s perfect! We believe in hiring people, not just a list of skills. We encourage you to apply if you think this is a role that would make you excited about coming to work every day.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring to the table...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of leadership experience within a Sales, Deal Strategy or Strategic Finance function.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MBA or Master’s Degree in Finance, Economics, or a related quantitative field.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep expertise in SaaS metrics (ARR), revenue recognition principles (ASC 606), and the lead-to-cash lifecycle.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record supporting high-growth enterprise software sales organizations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional interpersonal skills with the ability to influence cross-functional stakeholders and executive leadership.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen paired with superior analytical, problem-solving, and project management capabilities.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer-facing experience with the ability to articulate complex financial structures and principles clearly.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organized, customer-focused, innovative, and strong attention to detail&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to thrive under pressure and prioritize effectively during high-volume cycles.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About JFrog:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;JFrog is the only end-to-end software supply chain platform that provides complete visibility, security, and control for automating the delivery of trusted releases from code to production. Our platform enables organizations to manage, secure, and automate their software delivery process, fueling innovation without worry. We empower companies to build and release software faster and more securely than ever before.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With over 7,500 customers worldwide, including many Fortune 100 companies, JFrog is at the forefront of global innovation. Join us in shaping the future of software delivery and contributing to solutions that empower some of the world&#39;s most influential industries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Here’s what our employees have to say about working at JFrog:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;&quot;I wanted to work in a company that takes technology forward.&quot;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;&quot;Our business is so interesting because it is constantly moving, and we have to adapt new solutions to the challenges that arise from the customers.&quot;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;em&gt;&quot;It’s nice to work for a company with a must-have product, not a nice-to-have.&quot;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;#LI-REMOTE&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At JFrog, we’re reinventing DevSecOps to help the world’s greatest companies innovate. Our team of industry-leading software security experts is a true pioneer, constantly pushing the boundaries with original research and technological innovation. JFrog is a special place with a unique combination of brilliance, spirit, and just all-around great people. Thousands of customers, including the majority of the Fortune 100, trust JFrog to manage, accelerate, and secure their software delivery from code to production – a concept we call “liquid software”. Wouldn&#39;t it be amazing if you could join us on our journey?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;JFrog is seeking a Senior Financial Analyst to be the primary financial partner to our People (HR) and Operations organizations. Reporting to our Director of FP&amp;amp;A in Israel, you will be a business partner first and a modeler second. You’ll help HR and Ops leaders understand what their people&#39;s investments cost, what they return, and where the next shekel does the most good. Curiosity is the core of this role: you’ll understand how and where HR brings value to JFrog, why a number moved, go talk to the people behind it, and turn what you learn into a clear recommendation. You’ll work AI-first, using tools like Claude as part of your everyday analysis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a Senior FP&amp;amp;A at JFrog you will...&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HR Partnership:&lt;/strong&gt; Act as the day-to-day finance partner to HR leadership and HR business partners, translating people priorities into budget, headcount, and cost scenarios.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KPIs &amp;amp; People Analytics:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner closely with our HR Analysis organization to build and maintain the people and operations scorecard (headcount vs. plan, attrition and regretted attrition, time-to-fill, cost per hire, revenue per employee), and explain movements in plain language.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recruiting Planning:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with our VP of Recruiting to create the recruiting plan and budget: requisition planning, recruiter capacity, agency spend, cost per hire, and offer modeling. Act as a single point of contact around company headcount planning representing FP&amp;amp;A.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Workforce, Compensation &amp;amp; Benefits Planning:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner on annual headcount planning and in-year re-forecasts, building driver-based models in Pigment that link hiring plans to cost. Model merit and bonus cycles, equity refresh costs, benefits cost, and total rewards scenarios, and support comp reviews and pay-equity analysis with HR.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operations, Workplace &amp;amp; Executive Reporting:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Operations on workplace and facilities costs across Netanya and Tel Aviv (real estate analysis is secondary), and prepare monthly and quarterly people and operations reviews plus board-level materials for the Director of FP&amp;amp;A, the CFO, and HR leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To be a Senior FP&amp;amp;A at JFrog you need...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5–8 years&lt;/strong&gt; of progressive finance experience, including &lt;strong&gt;at least 3 years in a business partnering role&lt;/strong&gt; supporting HR, People, or Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Demonstrated experience as an HR partner:&lt;/strong&gt; you have sat in HR leadership meetings, owned people metrics, and influenced HR decisions with financial analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Prior direct partnership with HR and/or Operations teams&lt;/strong&gt;, ideally in a SaaS, tech, or other high-growth company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Genuine business curiosity and a people-oriented mindset:&lt;/strong&gt; you keep asking “why,” you enjoy learning how teams work, and you build trust with people who don’t speak finance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strong executive function:&lt;/strong&gt; highly organized, managing multiple priorities in a fast-paced, global environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on comp and benefits cost modeling:&lt;/strong&gt; merit, bonus, equity, and benefits costing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expert Excel and financial modeling&lt;/strong&gt;, with hands-on &lt;strong&gt;Pigment&lt;/strong&gt; experience required. &lt;strong&gt;Working experience with Oracle HCM&lt;/strong&gt; strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Excellent communication in both Hebrew and English&lt;/strong&gt;, able to distill complex financial concepts for non-finance audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-first working style:&lt;/strong&gt; daily hands-on use of Claude or similar AI tools to build models, analyze data, draft materials, and automate recurring reporting - Advantage&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with real estate, workplace, or facilities cost planning - Advantage&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Israeli employment cost components (pension, study fund, severance, statutory benefits) - Advantage&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At JFrog, we’re reinventing DevOps to help the world’s greatest companies innovate -- and we want you along for the ride. This is a special place with a unique combination of brilliance, spirit and just all-around great people. Here, if you’re willing to do more, your career can take off. And since software plays a central role in everyone’s lives, you’ll be part of an important mission. Thousands of customers, including the majority of the Fortune 100, trust JFrog to manage, accelerate, and secure their software delivery from code to production -- a concept we call “liquid software.” Wouldn&#39;t it be amazing if you could join us in our journey?&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;JFrog is seeking a Senior GTM FP&amp;amp;A Analyst to support our global Sales, Marketing, and Growth organizations. Reporting to the Director of Sales and Marketing FP&amp;amp;A, you will provide the financial modeling, forecasting, and executive reporting that underpin GTM investment decisions and performance management across Sales and Marketing. This is a hands-on, highly analytical role in a fast-paced SaaS environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role does require being onsite in our Sunnyvale Swamp 3 days a week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a Senior GTM FP&amp;amp;A Analyst at JFrog you will...&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support AOP, budgeting, and quarterly forecasting for GTM teams, covering headcount, commissions, and opex&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare monthly/quarterly budget-vs-actual analysis; partner with business owners to explain drivers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare and contribute to monthly reporting, QBRs, board-level metrics, and Marketing metrics packs for executive and CFO review&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain capacity planning and partner-pathway models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze Marketing spend efficiency and ROI, including CAC by channel and campaign/pipeline attribution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop executive-ready KPI packages and variance commentary for Director/VP and GTM leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build self-serve dashboards giving GTM leadership real-time visibility into key metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support business case analysis for GTM investments, tracking realized ROI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To be a Senior GTM FP&amp;amp;A Analyst at JFrog you need...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7-10 years FP&amp;amp;A experience; direct GTM Finance experience in SaaS preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Pigment, Anaplan, or comparable planning tools; familiarity with Power BI, Tableau, or similar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in SaaS FP&amp;amp;A, management consulting, or comparable background bridging financial and operational metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong SQL; advanced modeling (Excel/Sheets)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SaaS metrics fluency (ARR, NRR, Sales Efficiency, NDR, CAC payback)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity for AI/automation in FP&amp;amp;A workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preferred: experience working across time zones/geographies, or meaningful international exposure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written/verbal communication; able to distill complex analysis into crisp executive messaging&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to navigate cross-functional relationships (Finance, Accounting, Sales Ops) and drive alignment without formal authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT JFROG CAN OFFER…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At JFrog, base salary is only one component of our compensation package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position has a base salary range between $160,000 to $190,000. &amp;nbsp;Base salary will be based on your skills, qualifications, experience and location.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position also includes an equity package of restricted stock units (RSU). &amp;nbsp;In addition, JFrog employees are eligible to participate in our Employee Stock Purchase Plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JFrog provides employees comprehensive benefits including medical, dental, vision, retirement, wellness and much more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;JFrog is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation, national origin or nationality, ancestry, age, disability, gender identity or expression, marital status or any other category protected by law.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At JFrog, we’re reinventing DevSecOps to help the world’s greatest companies innovate. Our team of industry-leading software security experts is a true pioneer, constantly pushing the boundaries with original research and technological innovation. JFrog is a special place with a unique combination of brilliance, spirit, and just all-around great people. Thousands of customers, including the majority of the Fortune 100, trust JFrog to manage, accelerate, and secure their software delivery from code to production – a concept we call “liquid software”. Wouldn&#39;t it be amazing if you could join us on our journey?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Global Organizational Development Partner, you will design and implement strategic organizational, leadership, and talent development initiatives across the company worldwide. You will partner and collaborate with key stakeholders across all regions and ensure all programs are aligned with business goals. In addition to program design, you will personally facilitate executive and leadership team development, and lead complex change management efforts end-to-end.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a Global Organizational Development Partner you will...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and deliver global organization development strategies and solutions that align with JFrog&#39;s business objectives and drive JFrog&#39;s growth across all regions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and implement global strategies and approaches to identify, assess, and develop current and potential leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and personally facilitate executive and leadership team development sessions, offsites, and workshops&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Lead end-to-end change management for complex, cross-regional, multi-stakeholder initiatives — owning the strategy, plan, and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop engaging and innovative global talent and leadership development programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Develop, improve, and reinforce global strategies, structures, and processes — such as employee surveys, engagement processes, performance management, and more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive JFrog&#39;s unique culture transformation globally through targeted programs and initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with HR and business partners across regions to deliver consistent, integrated solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach and advise senior business partners and leaders on organization development topics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capture and share standards, best practices, external benchmarks, and innovative practices related to culture, change management, team effectiveness, strategy operationalization, organizational design, and organizational diagnosis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To be a &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Global Organizational Development Partner you need...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in organizational development in a global high-tech organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;Proven, hands-on experience designing and personally facilitating executive and leadership-team development sessions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant, demonstrated depth in change management able to independently lead complex, cross-regional change efforts from strategy to execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating globally across multiple regions and cultures in a dynamic, complex environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding communication, facilitation, interpersonal, and presentation skills, including with senior executives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At JFrog, we’re reinventing DevOps to help the world’s greatest companies innovate -- and we want you along for the ride. This is a special place with a unique combination of brilliance, spirit and just all-around great people. Here, if you’re willing to do more, your career can take off. And since software plays a central role in everyone’s lives, you’ll be part of an important mission. Thousands of customers, including the majority of the Fortune 100, trust JFrog to manage, accelerate, and secure their software delivery from code to production -- a concept we call “liquid software.” Wouldn&#39;t it be amazing if you could join us in our journey?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The position is based out of our &lt;strong&gt;Atlanta office.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our customers set a high bar. JFrog serves about 83% of the Fortune 100. That includes all of the Fortune 500’s top 10 technology and top 10 financial services companies, 8 of the top 10 retail companies, 8 of the top 10 healthcare companies, and all of the top 7 telecommunications companies. These customers bring heavily negotiated paper, demanding security and privacy requirements, and regulators of their own. You will work on a friendly, collaborative team that moves very fast, where each deal needs both speed and precision.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a Senior Legal Counsel, Commercial at JFrog you will...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be the sales team’s trusted deal partner. &lt;/strong&gt;Join deals early, give account teams clear and practical guidance, and escalate non-standard asks quickly with a clear recommendation.&amp;nbsp;Bring in compliance, finance, export control, and product experts when a customer request requires it, so deals close on time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Negotiate directly with enterprise and public sector customers.&lt;/strong&gt; Draft, review and negotiate SaaS, self-hosted and subscription agreements, order forms, reseller and partner agreements, and NDAs (many of these are on customer paper with sophisticated legal and procurement teams across the table.)&amp;nbsp;Advise sales leadership on limitations of liability, indemnities, IP and AI-related terms.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Respond to customer privacy demands.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Negotiate DPAs and privacy terms requested by customers.&amp;nbsp;Advise sales on obligations under the CCPA/CPRA, and other US state privacy laws.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Respond to customer security, resilience and incident requirements.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;Work closely with the security team to Negotiate information security addenda, DORA addenda, NIS2 flow-down terms, audit rights, and breach notification, cooperation and liability terms. Strong preference for candidate that managed cyber security incidents, participate in such programs, and advise management.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make the sales process faster. &lt;/strong&gt;Turn recurring customer requests into better templates, playbooks, approved fallback positions and self-service resources, so routine deals close without legal review.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support government and state customer deals. &lt;/strong&gt;Handle the contract terms public sector customers require, including FedRAMP, CMMC and secure software development attestation obligations. Work with our government channel partners and internal experts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To be a Senior Legal Counsel, Commercial at JFrog you need...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Law degree from an accredited US law school and admitted to practice in California or Georgia.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 8 years of relevant experience with a law firm and/or in-house legal department.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Substantive experience in commercial business transactions, including sales agreements; intellectual property related considerations including SaaS agreements, and risk allocation; independently managing and directing cross-border projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication and negotiation skills and ability to connect with, and gain the respect of, cross-functional stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent business sense and legal judgment with the ability to identify and escalate matters in a timely and concise manner..&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong negotiation skill, ability to command the room and to influence others without authority.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Capacity to interact and communicate with senior leadership and other stakeholders and remain adaptable in a changing business environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative approach and the interest in working in a fast-paced, team-oriented environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superior organizational skills and attention to detail with a mindset that processes can always be improved.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High integrity and professionalism, strong sense of ownership, and eagerness to learn.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT JFROG CAN OFFER…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At JFrog, base salary is only one component of our compensation package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position has a base salary range between $190k to $205k.&amp;nbsp; Base salary will be based on your skills, qualifications, experience and location.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position also includes an equity package of restricted stock units (RSU).&amp;nbsp; In addition, JFrog employees are eligible to participate in our Employee Stock Purchase Plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JFrog provides employees comprehensive benefits including medical, dental, vision, retirement, wellness and much more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JFrog embraces hybrid work: 3 days in office / 2 days remote.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;JFrog is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation, national origin or nationality, ancestry, age, disability, gender identity or expression, marital status or any other category protected by law.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At JFrog, we’re reinventing DevSecOps to help the world’s greatest companies innovate.&amp;nbsp;Our team of industry-leading software security experts is a true pioneer, constantly pushing the boundaries with original research and technological innovation.&amp;nbsp;JFrog is a special place with a unique combination of brilliance, spirit, and just all-around great people.&amp;nbsp;Thousands of customers, including the majority of the Fortune 100, trust JFrog to manage, accelerate, and secure their software delivery from code to production – a concept we call “liquid software”. Wouldn&#39;t it be amazing if you could join us on our journey?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an Offensive Security Engineer, you will spearhead JFrog’s offensive security operations and lead advanced threat research initiatives, playing a pivotal role in safeguarding our organization and customers from evolving cyber threats. You will develop and execute Red Team exercises, simulate real-world attacks, and identify security weaknesses in JFrog’s systems and applications. We seek a highly skilled, proactive tech leader who thrives in challenging environments and is passionate about advancing security research and offensive strategies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As an &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Offensive Security Engineer,&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; you will…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, plan, design, and execute Red Team operations, threat modeling, and adversarial simulations against JFrog’s infrastructure and cloud environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive threat research and intelligence initiatives to stay ahead of emerging cyber threats, attack techniques, and vulnerabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute advanced attack scenarios to assess security defenses and provide actionable recommendations for improving JFrog’s security posture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with security engineering, DevOps, and software development teams to implement findings and enhance our defenses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the development of tooling, frameworks, and methodologies to automate and optimize Red Team exercises.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor and guide a team of security professionals, fostering a culture of innovation, collaboration, and continuous learning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in incident responses when Red Team exercises reveal vulnerabilities, providing expertise on attack techniques, forensics, and post-attack mitigation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Continuously assess and improve security processes, playbooks, and threat detection mechanisms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To be an&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Offensive Security Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; at JFrog, you need…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in offensive security operations, Red Teaming, threat hunting, or threat research&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of attack techniques, TTPs (Tactics, Techniques, and Procedures), adversary simulations, and threat-hunting methodologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with Red Team tools, frameworks (e.g., Metasploit, Cobalt Strike, Burp Suite), and custom exploit development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience with cloud platforms (AWS, GCP, Azure) and containerized environments (Kubernetes, Docker)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with the MITRE ATT&amp;amp;CK Framework and its application in Red Team and threat-hunting scenarios&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with scripting and automation languages for tool development, threat detection, and attack simulation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of offensive security best practices, vulnerability management, threat detection, and advanced threat analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to effectively communicate and collaborate with cross-functional teams, translating complex security concepts into actionable insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A passion for continuous learning, research, and innovation in the fields of offensive security, threat hunting, and cyber threats&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

