&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Partner Sales Manager – Australia &amp;amp; New Zealand (Channel Sales)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Location: Melbourne, Australia (Remote)&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;Fast-Frogward Your Career to Years From Now...&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;Be part of a team where your work directly shapes the way the world&#39;s leading organizations&lt;br&gt;build and secure their software. JFrog is seeking a dynamic, results-driven Senior Partner Sales&lt;br&gt;Manager to lead and expand our partner ecosystem across Australia and New Zealand.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is a strategic, quota-carrying role focused on driving revenue through partners, developing&lt;br&gt;high-performing alliances, and accelerating pipeline growth. You will work closely with leading&lt;br&gt;Global and Regional System Integrators, Cloud Service Providers, Distributors, and Technology&lt;br&gt;Alliances to build scalable go-to-market initiatives and deliver measurable business outcomes.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;● Drive partner-sourced and partner-influenced revenue across Australia and New&lt;br&gt;Zealand, with a strong focus on new logo acquisition, expansion opportunities, and&lt;br&gt;renewals.&lt;br&gt;● Develop and execute Joint Business Plans (JBPs) with strategic partners aligned to&lt;br&gt;regional growth objectives.&lt;br&gt;● Build executive relationships across AU and NZ Regional SIs, Global System Integrators&lt;br&gt;(GSIs) Value Added Resellers (VARs), Cloud Partners, and Distributors.&lt;br&gt;● Work closely with the direct sales organization to drive co-selling motions and joint&lt;br&gt;account planning.&lt;br&gt;● Generate qualified pipeline through partner-led demand generation, workshops,&lt;br&gt;enablement sessions, executive briefings, and industry events.&lt;br&gt;● Recruit, onboard, and enable new strategic partners to strengthen JFrog&#39;s market&lt;br&gt;coverage across enterprise, commercial, public sector, and regulated industries.&lt;br&gt;● Drive partner enablement, sales accreditation, and technical certifications to increase&lt;br&gt;partner capabilities and self-sufficiency.&lt;br&gt;● Conduct Quarterly Business Reviews (QBRs) with strategic partners and executive&lt;br&gt;stakeholders to review performance, pipeline, investments, and growth plans.&lt;br&gt;● Collaborate with Marketing on partner campaigns, field events, webinars, and&lt;br&gt;account-based marketing initiatives.&lt;br&gt;● Manage forecasting, opportunity progression, partner registrations, and partner pipeline&lt;br&gt;through Salesforce CRM.&lt;br&gt;● Work closely with Distribution partners to accelerate partner recruitment, enablement,&lt;br&gt;and regional expansion.&lt;br&gt;● Support commercial negotiations, opportunity strategy, partner agreements, and deal&lt;br&gt;execution.&lt;br&gt;● Develop strong relationships with hyperscalers including AWS, Microsoft Azure, and&lt;br&gt;Google Cloud to identify joint customer opportunities.&lt;br&gt;● Stay current with market trends including DevSecOps, Software Supply Chain Security,&lt;br&gt;AI, Cloud Native technologies, and Cybersecurity.&lt;br&gt;Preferred Partner Ecosystem Experience&lt;br&gt;Experience working with one or more of the following partner types is highly desirable:&lt;br&gt;● Regional System Integrators&lt;br&gt;● Global System Integrators (NTT DATA, Infosys, TCS, Accenture, Avanade)&lt;br&gt;● Value Added Resellers&lt;br&gt;● Cloud Solution Providers&lt;br&gt;● Software Distributors&lt;br&gt;● DevOps Consulting Partners&lt;br&gt;● Cloud Native and Kubernetes specialists&lt;br&gt;● Security Consulting Partners&lt;br&gt;● AWS, Microsoft Azure and Google Cloud Partner ecosystems&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;● Bachelor&#39;s degree in Business, Engineering, Computer Science, Information Technology,&lt;br&gt;or related discipline. MBA is advantageous.&lt;br&gt;● 7+ years of experience in Channel Sales, Alliances, Partner Management, or Business&lt;br&gt;Development within Enterprise Software, Cybersecurity, DevOps, Cloud, or SaaS.&lt;br&gt;● Demonstrated success managing quota and delivering measurable revenue growth&lt;br&gt;through partners.&lt;br&gt;● Experience working with enterprise customers and complex multi-million-dollar&lt;br&gt;opportunities.&lt;br&gt;● Strong understanding of enterprise software sales cycles within the Australian and New&lt;br&gt;Zealand markets.&lt;br&gt;● Knowledge of DevOps, DevSecOps, Software Supply Chain Security, CI/CD, Cloud&lt;br&gt;Native technologies, Containers, Kubernetes, or Application Security is highly desirable.&lt;br&gt;● Excellent executive communication, presentation, negotiation, and relationship-building&lt;br&gt;skills.&lt;br&gt;● Strong business planning, forecasting, and analytical capabilities.&lt;br&gt;● Experience with Salesforce CRM and partner management processes.&lt;br&gt;● Ability to work cross-functionally with Sales, Customer Success, Marketing, Sales&lt;br&gt;Engineering, Legal, Finance, and Product teams.&lt;br&gt;● Self-starter capable of managing multiple strategic initiatives in a fast-paced&lt;br&gt;environment.&lt;br&gt;● Willingness to travel across Australia and New Zealand.&lt;br&gt;What You&#39;ll Bring&lt;br&gt;● Proven ability to build, influence, and grow high-performing partner ecosystems.&lt;br&gt;● Strong executive presence with experience engaging C-level stakeholders across&lt;br&gt;partners and customers.&lt;br&gt;● Strategic thinking combined with hands-on execution.&lt;br&gt;● Commercial acumen and experience building joint go-to-market strategies.&lt;br&gt;● Passion for cloud technologies, DevSecOps, and helping customers modernize software&lt;br&gt;delivery securely.&lt;br&gt;● Collaborative mindset with the ability to influence across regional and global teams.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why JFrog?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;At JFrog, we enable organizations to build, secure, distribute, and manage software at&lt;br&gt;enterprise scale. Our Software Supply Chain Platform powers many of the world&#39;s most&lt;br&gt;innovative companies, helping them deliver trusted software faster and more securely.&lt;br&gt;As part of the ANZ team, you&#39;ll have the opportunity to shape JFrog&#39;s partner strategy across&lt;br&gt;one of our fastest-growing regions, working alongside leading cloud providers, technology&lt;br&gt;partners, and system integrators to accelerate customer success.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;If you&#39;re passionate about building strategic partnerships, driving business growth, and helping&lt;br&gt;enterprises transform how they deliver software, we&#39;d love to hear from you. Apply today and&lt;br&gt;help shape the future of Software Supply Chain Security with JFrog.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;#LI-REMOTE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/article&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fast-Frogward Your Career to Years From Now&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;Be part of a team where your work takes center stage, shaping the future of software development. At JFrog, we solve critical challenges for leaders like Amazon, Google, and Netflix. Every day brings opportunities to innovate and push boundaries in a fast-moving, frogward-thinking culture. If you want your work to matter and thrive on nonstop innovation, JFrog is your place.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Here’s what our employees have to say about working at JFrog:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot; data-start=&quot;472&quot; data-end=&quot;581&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-start=&quot;472&quot; data-end=&quot;581&quot;&gt;&quot;I get to solve complex platform challenges that impact thousands of developers and enterprises worldwide.&quot;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot; data-start=&quot;586&quot; data-end=&quot;722&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-start=&quot;586&quot; data-end=&quot;722&quot;&gt;&quot;Product decisions here are driven by customer problems, not just roadmaps. We have the autonomy to shape the future of the platform.&quot;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot; data-start=&quot;727&quot; data-end=&quot;900&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-start=&quot;727&quot; data-end=&quot;900&quot;&gt;&quot;Working alongside world-class engineering teams allows us to build secure, scalable capabilities—from identity and access management to AI-powered developer experiences.&quot;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;p data-pm-slice=&quot;1 1 []&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;We are looking for an experienced &lt;strong&gt;Senior Product Manager&lt;/strong&gt; to drive product strategy, discovery, and execution across our security and enterprise software portfolio. In this role, you will own products and features throughout their lifecycle, translate customer and market needs into impactful solutions, and collaborate closely with engineering and cross-functional teams to deliver secure, scalable, customer-focused products.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll be doing as a Senior Product Manager :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own the end-to-end product lifecycle&lt;/strong&gt;, from ideation, discovery, and market research to product strategy, roadmap definition, development, launch, and ongoing optimization.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define product vision and strategy&lt;/strong&gt; by understanding customer needs, market trends, competitive landscapes, and business objectives, particularly in enterprise software and security.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive product discovery and execution&lt;/strong&gt; by translating customer problems and business requirements into clear product specifications, user stories, and prioritized roadmaps.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate closely with Engineering and R&amp;amp;D&lt;/strong&gt; to evaluate technical feasibility, make informed trade-offs, and deliver scalable, reliable, and secure solutions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Champion security-focused innovation&lt;/strong&gt; by identifying opportunities to strengthen application security, software supply chain security, vulnerability management, and developer-focused security capabilities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Act as the voice of the customer&lt;/strong&gt;, engaging with enterprise customers, sales, support, and other stakeholders to gather feedback, validate solutions, and drive product adoption.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead cross-functional alignment&lt;/strong&gt; with Product Marketing, Sales, Customer Success, Support, and other business teams to ensure successful product launches and feature adoption.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use data and product metrics&lt;/strong&gt; to measure product performance, evaluate business impact, and continuously improve customer experience and product outcomes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Influence stakeholders across the organization&lt;/strong&gt; and communicate product strategy, priorities, progress, and results effectively to leadership and global teams.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring on to the table:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;12+ years of overall professional experience&lt;/strong&gt;, with at least &lt;strong&gt;6 years of hands-on Product Management experience&lt;/strong&gt; in the software industry.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;Proven experience owning and delivering complex B2B enterprise software products, preferably SaaS platforms or developer-focused products.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;Strong understanding of &lt;strong&gt;application security, software security, or cybersecurity concepts&lt;/strong&gt;, with experience translating security challenges into product capabilities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;Experience defining product strategy, managing roadmaps, conducting product discovery, prioritizing features, and driving end-to-end product execution.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;Ability to translate complex customer and business requirements into clear product requirements, specifications, and user stories for Engineering and QA teams.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;Experience working closely with Engineering and R&amp;amp;D teams on technically complex products, balancing customer needs, technical feasibility, scalability, and business priorities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;Strong understanding of enterprise customers, their business challenges, and the requirements of large-scale software environments.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;Excellent stakeholder management, communication, and analytical skills, with the ability to influence cross-functional teams without formal authority.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;Demonstrated ability to manage multiple priorities, drive alignment across teams, and deliver measurable product and business outcomes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;A bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related technical field, or equivalent hands-on experience in software development or technical product management.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4 data-pm-slice=&quot;1 3 []&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;Good to have&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;Experience with &lt;strong&gt;JFrog Artifactory&lt;/strong&gt; or other artifact management and binary repository solutions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;Experience in the &lt;strong&gt;DevOps ecosystem&lt;/strong&gt;, including CI/CD pipelines, software delivery, developer tools, or platform engineering.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;Knowledge of software supply chain security, vulnerability scanning, open-source security, SBOMs, or related security practices.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About JFrog:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;JFrog is the only end-to-end software supply chain platform that provides complete visibility, security, and control for automating the delivery of trusted releases from code to production. Our platform enables organizations to manage, secure, and automate their software delivery process, fueling innovation without worry. We empower companies to build and release software faster and more securely than ever before.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;With over 7,500 customers worldwide, including many Fortune 100 companies, JFrog is at the forefront of global innovation. Join us in shaping the future of software delivery and contributing to solutions that empower some of the world&#39;s most influential industries.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NOTE: The job location is Bangalore (Bellandur) and we follow a hybrid model, mandatory 3 days/week work from office.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Product Manager - Artifactory Packages&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At JFrog, we’re reinventing DevOps to help the world’s greatest companies innovate -- and we want you along for the ride. This is a special place with a unique combination of brilliance, spirit, and just all-around great people. Here, if you’re willing to do more, your career can take off. And since software plays a central role in everyone’s lives, you’ll be part of an important mission. Thousands of customers, including the majority of the Fortune 100, trust JFrog to manage, accelerate, and secure their software delivery from code to production -- a concept we call “liquid software.” Wouldn&#39;t it be amazing if you could join us on our journey?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Product Manager to join our Artifactory Packages product group. You will drive product strategy and execution across a broad Packages area and multiple engineering teams, helping developers and platform teams onboard and work with package ecosystems through Artifactory. While our solutions empower the world&#39;s largest enterprises, we know that an exceptional developer experience must be native to modern workflows, bridging the power of the traditional terminal with the agility of intelligent coding assistants. Your mission goes beyond building for companies; you will be dedicated to giving each and every software developer the absolute best, frictionless native experience. You will drive satisfaction by bridging massive scale with intuitive, developer-first tooling, ensuring everyone, from the individual coder to the global platform team, gets an exceptional experience working with the JFrog Platform. This is an individual-contributor role with influence beyond a single backlog or delivery team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a Senior Product Manager at JFrog you will…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the full cycle of product development for a broad Packages area, from strategy and discovery through launch, monitoring, and growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with multiple engineering teams to manage concurrent initiatives, balance priorities, and make tradeoffs against user and business outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own several different integration paths with JFrog Artifactory, delivering a coherent experience for admins and developers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-core and cross-region collaborations that advance JFrog success across DevOps, Security, and Governance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define product vision and strategy from customer needs, market opportunities, and product evidence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Engineering, Product Analysts, UX/UI, Product Marketing, Sales, Support, and other partners to deliver B2D products and meet customer and business goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define customer and business outcomes, track adoption and usage, and iterate using customer and product evidence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align senior stakeholders and get buy-in for the product vision across internal and external partners without relying on formal authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To be a Senior Product Manager at JFrog you need…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of end-to-end Product Management experience in a B2B / B2D or enterprise technology environment, with repeated ownership across multiple product scopes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience balancing and prioritizing multiple initiatives across teams, with tradeoffs tied to user and business outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shipping coherent product experiences across different technical integration paths&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with customers, users, buyers, and decision makers on user-facing products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing PRDs and leading engineering partners on prioritization and delivery across multiple teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to set direction under ambiguity and influence cross-functional partners without formal authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and spoken English for daily work with global and distributed teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical experience in Programming, Engineering, Security, DevOps, SRE, Tech Support, or another hands-on technical domain - a huge advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: georgia, palatino, serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NOTE: The job location is Bangalore (Bellandur) and we follow a hybrid model, mandatory 3 days/week work from office.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;At JFrog, we’re reinventing DevOps to help the world’s greatest companies innovate -- and we want you along for the ride. This is a special place with a unique combination of brilliance, spirit and just all-around great people. Here, if you’re willing to do more, your career can take off. And since software plays a central role in everyone’s lives, you’ll be part of an important mission. Thousands of customers, including the majority of the Fortune 100, trust JFrog to manage, accelerate, and secure their software delivery from code to production -- a concept we call “liquid software.” Wouldn&#39;t it be amazing if you could join us in our journey?&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you love working with brilliant people, being part of an energetic team, changing the world of software and you’ve got the technical skills, you might be the perfect Frog to join our Swamp! Come and join the Professional Services team and help us to continue to lead the rapidly evolving space of DevOps and DevSecOps!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;As a Senior Professional Services DevOps Engineer in JFrog you will...&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with JFrog customers to design, setup and build CI/CD pipelines and DevOps platform using JFrog products and other cutting edge technologies and practices like Docker, Kubernetes, IaC and Cloud Native&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team up with Sales, Customer Success, Support and Development while work directly with Devs and DevOps Pros to ensure success with the customer’s DevOps journey using the JFrog platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Setup, design and build CI pipelines with Docker, NPM, Java, Pypi etc.. (Binary Repositories, Distribution to Devices and Continuous Build Tooling)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Train the open source community and JFrog customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence the features and roadmap of JFrog tools based on customer needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep current with the latest technology trends related to DevOps and the landscape of CI/CD Technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with our customers and community to build solid relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To be a Senior Professional Services DevOps Engineer in JFrog you need...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years experience with Continuous Integration tools: CI Server, Git, Artifactory, Jenkins, Maven, Docker, NPM&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build software delivery pipelines with Docker, npm, Java, Pypi etc.. with various DevOps tools such as Git, Binary repositories management, Binary scanning, and Continuous integration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good understanding of infrastructure &amp;amp; operations - storage, network, computer, security, cloud (public, on-prem)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Continuous Deployment and Delivery tools: Chef, Puppet, Ansible, Kubernetes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands on experience in Linux - Mandatory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands on experience with cloud infrastructure - AWS / Azure / GCP - Mandatory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with customer facing with great interpersonal and customer service oriented skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with server side software on-premise and in the cloud&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Software Architecture design and product development a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uncompromising will to learn&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Open Source state-of-mind&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT JFROG CAN OFFER…&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At JFrog, base salary is only one component of our compensation package.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position has a base salary range between $150,000 to $180,000. &amp;nbsp;Base salary will be based on your skills, qualifications, experience and location.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Additionally, this role may be eligible for discretionary bonuses or commission payments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position also includes an equity package of restricted stock units (RSU). &amp;nbsp;In addition, JFrog employees are eligible to participate in our Employee Stock Purchase Plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;JFrog provides employees comprehensive benefits including medical, dental, vision, retirement, wellness and much more!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;JFrog is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, creed, religion, sex, sexual orientation, national origin or nationality, ancestry, age, disability, gender identity or expression, marital status or any other category protected by law.&lt;/p&gt;

