&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary tool administrator for our project management stack, including expert-level configuration and management of Jira and ClickUp.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with cross-functional partners —including developers, designers, content creators, and marketing stakeholders—and our Senior Web Strategist to align on project goals, creative and technical requirements, and timelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement, and continuously improve our web operational governance model to ensure consistency, efficiency, and quality across all projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the web team&#39;s roadmap, facilitate prioritization, and oversee resource allocation to ensure strategic goals are met.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead agile ceremonies, including sprint planning, daily stand-ups, retrospectives, and backlog grooming sessions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Utilize data and analytics to report on project velocity, team performance, and operational efficiency, identifying opportunities for process improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To be a Technical Program Manager at JFrog you need . . .&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5-7+ years of experience in program or technical project management, with a strong focus on managing complex web projects in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert-level knowledge and proven success implementing and managing Scrum, Kanban, and Waterfall project management processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A deep understanding of the web project lifecycle, including both the technical and creative requirements needed to bring digital experiences to life.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional proficiency with modern project management tools, specifically Jira and ClickUp, with a strong ability to configure workflows, build dashboards, and train users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Outstanding communication, negotiation, and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to translate complex operational needs into clear, actionable plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A data-driven and process-oriented mindset, with a passion for continuous improvement and optimizing team workflows for maximum efficiency and quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
